# codex-system-test
"""# HTML Element Traceability

## Overview

This executable system specification traces ten HTML elements that were omitted
or overstated by the historical inventory report. It follows each element from
the canonical HTML tree through Web semantics, computed style, layout, Draw IR,
and Engine2D pixels.

The covered elements are `h1` through `h6`, `sub`, `sup`, `selectedcontent`,
and `slot`. A name appearing in a source file or manifest is not enough. Every
supported row needs semantic identity and a rendering oracle. Unsupported
behavior needs an explicit fail-closed oracle.

The scenarios use stable component IDs so a failure can be attributed to the
tree, style, layout, Draw IR, or raster stage. They do not use screenshots,
tolerance comparisons, or browser-dependent host fonts.

**Plan:** doc/03_plan/sys_test/html_css_spec_traceability.md

**Requirements:** doc/02_requirements/feature/simple_web_browser_engine_production_hardening.md

**NFR:** doc/02_requirements/nfr/simple_web_browser_engine_production_hardening.md

**Design:** N/A

The exact production owners and frozen oracles are defined by the plan above.

**Research:** N/A

The retained WHATWG-derived corpus row and hash are embedded below.

## Requirement Traceability

- `REQ-WEB-BROWSER-002` requires canonical HTML tree and semantic behavior.
- `REQ-WEB-BROWSER-004` requires Web layout to lower through Draw IR and
  Engine2D rather than a private rendering shortcut.
- `REQ-WEB-BROWSER-019` requires pinned corpus accounting.
- `REQ-WEB-BROWSER-021` requires executable SSpec evidence and a current
  generated manual.

The top-level `@req` declarations bind all three scenarios to those four
requirements. Each scenario repeats the requirement tags in its authored
manual metadata so generated documentation remains traceable.

## Canonical Production Path

The semantic oracle is built by `html_tree_builder_build` and queried through
the BeDOM accessors. The rendered oracle uses
`simple_web_layout_render_html_draw_ir_result`.

That renderer produces one shared result containing Web semantic nodes,
computed styles, layout boxes, and `DrawIrComposition`. The test then sends the
composition to `Engine2dCompositorBackend` for exact pixel evidence.

No scenario invokes a GUI-only renderer, an HTML fallback painter, a private
font path, or a Rust bootstrap seed. Visible content must remain attributable
to the canonical Web-to-Draw-IR path.

## Selected User-Agent Profile

The selected profile uses a 16 px medium font. Relative heading sizes and
margins use round-half-up.

| Element | Font size | Block-start/end margin | Exact geometry |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| `h1` | 32 px | 21 px | `[0,21,96,32]` |
| `h2` | 24 px | 20 px | `[0,20,96,24]` |
| `h3` | 19 px | 19 px | `[0,19,96,19]` |
| `h4` | 16 px | 21 px | `[0,21,96,16]` |
| `h5` | 13 px | 22 px | `[0,22,96,13]` |
| `h6` | 11 px | 26 px | `[0,26,96,11]` |

The heading backgrounds use distinct colors. This makes a nonzero exact-color
pixel count a discriminating Engine2D oracle rather than a generic
"something rendered" check.

## Inline Metric Profile

The inline control uses geometry `[0,8,8,16]`. `sub` and `sup` use a 13 px
smaller font and reset inherited non-normal line height back to `normal`.

The exact subscript geometry is `[8,12,7,13]`. The exact superscript geometry
is `[15,4,7,13]`. Their text commands have Y coordinates `12` and `4`, while
the control text command has Y coordinate `8`.

The four-pixel shifts are based on the parent font size. The separate 24 px
parent line-height control proves that `sub` does not accidentally inherit an
authored non-normal line height.

## Customizable Select Policy

`selectedcontent` is currently classified `unsupported-fail-closed`. This does
not claim selected-option reflection.

Fail-closed hiding applies only when all selected validity conditions hold:

1. The parent is a `button`.
2. The button is the first element child of a non-`multiple` `select`.
3. The empty `selectedcontent` is the button's first child.

The valid control authors a red background and dimensions. The computed style
must still be `display:none`; no Draw IR command or red pixel may survive.

Three invalid-context controls prevent an overly broad hidden-tag rule. A
button after an option, a button in a `multiple` select, and a selectedcontent
after another button child all retain generic inline semantics and produce
their own Draw IR commands.

## Slot Fallback Policy

`slot` uses generic inline flow in this renderer. Because Shadow DOM slot
assignment is not active in this fixture, its fallback text must remain
visible through the ordinary Web semantic and Draw IR path.

The pinned slot geometry is `[0,32,104,16]`. Its computed foreground is decimal
ARGB `4286331629`, equivalent to `0xFF7C3AED`. The composition must contain the
fallback text and Engine2D must produce at least one matching purple pixel.

## Syntax

Run this source through the repository's normal SSpec runner with the canonical
pure-Simple target binary:

```sh
bin/release/simple test test/03_system/feature/web_platform/html/html_element_traceability_spec.spl --mode=native
```

This command is documentation only. Generated manuals do not claim execution;
qualified runner evidence is owned by the traceability gate.

To regenerate only this manual with an already-built mini docgen, provide the
source spec and canonical `doc/06_spec` destination to that tool. Do not place
executable `.spl` files under `doc/06_spec`.

## Examples

### Heading evidence

Given an isolated `<h2 id='heading-h2'>H</h2>`, the semantic node remains an
`h2` child of `body`, its computed font size is 24, both block margins are 20,
its Draw IR geometry is `[0,20,96,24]`, and its unique background reaches the
pixel buffer.

### Inline evidence

Given `A<sub>B</sub><sup>C</sup>` at 16 px, the three text-command Y coordinates
are `[8,12,4]`. Equality is intentional: merely checking relative order could
hide a wrong baseline magnitude.

### Fail-closed evidence

Given a valid empty `selectedcontent` as the first child of the first button in
a non-multiple select, authored `display:block` and red background do not make
it render. Moving the button or selectedcontent out of that exact context keeps
the element inline, proving invalid uses were not globally suppressed.

### Slot evidence

Given `<slot id='slot'>slot-fallback</slot>`, the fallback string appears in a
Draw IR text command and purple pixels. A semantic-only node without visible
fallback output is a failure.

## Failure Interpretation

- A missing BeDOM node or wrong parent is a tokenizer/tree/semantic failure.
- A wrong display, size, margin, line height, or vertical alignment is a style
  default or cascade failure.
- A wrong box or text Y coordinate is a layout failure.
- A missing component command or computed-style property is a Draw IR lowering
  failure.
- A correct command with no discriminating pixel is an Engine2D failure.
- A visible valid-context selectedcontent is a fail-closed policy failure.
- A hidden invalid-context selectedcontent is an overmatching policy failure.
- A corpus hash mismatch means the selected evidence row changed and requires
  an explicit review rather than silent acceptance.

## Evidence Boundaries

This spec proves the selected deterministic profile only. It does not claim
complete WHATWG rendering conformance, customizable-select reflection, Shadow
DOM distribution, platform-native widget parity, or qualified release-runner
admission.

The embedded corpus row is dated `2026-07-29` and names the ten covered
elements. `_expect_pinned_html_corpus` checks its SHA-256 and also checks an
altered-row negative control.

The generated manual is explanatory evidence. The executable assertions in
this source remain authoritative.
"""

use std.spec.*
use std.common.crypto.sha256.{sha256_text}
use common.ui.draw_ir.{DrawIrCommand, DrawIrComposition}
use os.compositor.compositor_engine2d.{Engine2dCompositorBackend}
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.dom.{BeDomNode}
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.dom_accessors.{
    be_dom_get_tag, be_dom_path_for_route
}
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.html_tree_builder.{
    html_tree_builder_build
}
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_html_layout_renderer.{
    HNode, SimpleWebLayoutDrawIrResult,
    simple_web_layout_render_html_draw_ir_result
}
use test.system.browser_dom_identity_helpers.{system_dom_identity_index, system_dom_route}

val WIDTH: i32 = 96
val HEIGHT: i32 = 256
val HTML_CORPUS_ROW = (
    "whatwg-html-elements|2026-07-29|" +
    "h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6,sub,sup,selectedcontent,slot|" +
    "medium=16px;round=half-up;" +
    "selectedcontent=unsupported-fail-closed"
)
val HTML_CORPUS_SHA256 = (
    "bd8cba62a4ed894e8a5ef3636c7f657ae974ecda1eb4da401d535b5279131e84"
)

fn _node_index(nodes: [HNode], component_id: text) -> i32:
    var index = 0
    for node in nodes:
        if node.id_attr == component_id:
            return index
        index = index + 1
    fail("missing Web semantic node: {component_id}")
    -1

fn _command_index(
    composition: DrawIrComposition, component_id: text
) -> i32:
    if composition.batches.len() == 0:
        fail("missing Draw IR batch")
    var index = 0
    for command in composition.batches[0].commands:
        if command.component_id == component_id:
            return index
        index = index + 1
    -1

fn _command(
    composition: DrawIrComposition, component_id: text
) -> DrawIrCommand:
    val index = _command_index(composition, component_id)
    if index < 0:
        fail("missing Draw IR command: {component_id}")
    composition.batches[0].commands[index]

fn _has_text(composition: DrawIrComposition, value: text) -> bool:
    for batch in composition.batches:
        for command in batch.commands:
            if (
                command.kind == "text" and
                command.text_value.contains(value)
            ):
                return true
    false

fn _text_command(
    composition: DrawIrComposition, value: text
) -> DrawIrCommand:
    for batch in composition.batches:
        for command in batch.commands:
            if (
                command.kind == "text" and
                command.text_value == value
            ):
                return command
    fail("missing Draw IR text command: {value}")
    composition.batches[0].commands[0]

fn _style(command: DrawIrCommand, key: text) -> text:
    for property in command.computed_style:
        if property.key == key:
            return property.value
    fail("missing Draw IR computed style: {key}")
    ""

fn _count_color(pixels: [u32], color: u32) -> i32:
    var count = 0
    for pixel in pixels:
        if pixel == color:
            count = count + 1
    count

fn _expect_semantic_identity(
    html: text, component_id: text, tag: text, parent_id: text
):
    val root = html_tree_builder_build(html)
    val identity_index = system_dom_identity_index(root)
    val path = be_dom_path_for_route(
        root, identity_index, system_dom_route(identity_index, component_id)
    )
    val parent_path = be_dom_path_for_route(
        root, identity_index, system_dom_route(identity_index, parent_id)
    )
    expect(path.len()).to_be_greater_than(1)
    expect(parent_path.len()).to_be_greater_than(0)
    val node: BeDomNode = path[path.len() - 1]
    val parent: BeDomNode = parent_path[parent_path.len() - 1]
    expect(be_dom_get_tag(node)).to_equal(tag)
    expect(node.node_id).to_be_greater_than(0)
    expect(node.parent_id).to_equal(parent.node_id)
    expect(path[path.len() - 2].node_id).to_equal(parent.node_id)

fn _expect_exact_draw_ir_geometry(
    result: SimpleWebLayoutDrawIrResult, component_id: text,
    parent_id: text, expected_tag: text, expected: [i32]
):
    if expected.len() != 4:
        fail("expected geometry must contain x, y, width, height")
    val node_index = _node_index(result.hit_index.nodes, component_id)
    val parent_index = result.hit_index.nodes[node_index].parent.to_i32()
    if parent_index < 0:
        fail("Web semantic node has no parent: {component_id}")
    expect(result.hit_index.nodes[parent_index].id_attr).to_equal(parent_id)
    val command = _command(result.composition, component_id)
    expect(command.parent_id).to_equal(parent_id)
    expect(_style(command, "tag")).to_equal(expected_tag)
    expect([
        result.hit_index.boxes.bx[node_index],
        result.hit_index.boxes.by[node_index],
        result.hit_index.boxes.bw[node_index],
        result.hit_index.boxes.bh[node_index]
    ]).to_equal(expected)
    expect([
        command.x, command.y, command.width, command.height
    ]).to_equal(expected)
    expect([
        command.clip_rect.x, command.clip_rect.y,
        command.clip_rect.width, command.clip_rect.height
    ]).to_equal([0, 0, WIDTH, HEIGHT])

fn _render_pixels(composition: DrawIrComposition) -> [u32]:
    val raster = Engine2dCompositorBackend.create_named(
        WIDTH, HEIGHT, "software"
    )
    val rendered = raster.render_draw_ir_composition(composition, [])
    raster.shutdown()
    expect(rendered.skipped_command_count).to_equal(0)
    expect(rendered.pixels.len()).to_equal(WIDTH * HEIGHT)
    rendered.pixels

fn _expect_pinned_html_corpus():
    expect(sha256_text(HTML_CORPUS_ROW)).to_equal(HTML_CORPUS_SHA256)
    expect(
        sha256_text(HTML_CORPUS_ROW + "|forged") == HTML_CORPUS_SHA256
    ).to_equal(false)

describe "Production HTML element traceability":
    # @manual: show
    # @capture(html)
    # @capture(protocol)
    # @capture(gui)
    it "should retain h1 through h6 with selected block heading metrics":
        # @req: REQ-WEB-BROWSER-002 REQ-WEB-BROWSER-004 REQ-WEB-BROWSER-019 REQ-WEB-BROWSER-021
        step("Trace HTML elements through Web semantics and Draw IR")
        _expect_pinned_html_corpus()
        val ids = ["h1", "h2", "h3", "h4", "h5", "h6"]
        val tags = ["h1", "h2", "h3", "h4", "h5", "h6"]
        val font_sizes = [32, 24, 19, 16, 13, 11]
        val margins = [21, 20, 19, 21, 22, 26]
        val colors = [
            0xFFDC2626u32, 0xFFEA580Cu32, 0xFFCA8A04u32,
            0xFF16A34Au32, 0xFF2563EBu32, 0xFF7C3AEDu32
        ]
        val color_hex = [
            "dc2626", "ea580c", "ca8a04",
            "16a34a", "2563eb", "7c3aed"
        ]
        var index = 0
        while index < ids.len():
            val html = (
                "<style>html,body{{margin:0}}</style><body id='body'><" +
                tags[index] + " id='" + ids[index] +
                "' style='background:#" + color_hex[index] +
                "'>H</" + tags[index] + "></body>"
            )
            val result = simple_web_layout_render_html_draw_ir_result(
                html, WIDTH, HEIGHT
            )
            _expect_semantic_identity(
                html, ids[index], tags[index], "body"
            )
            _expect_exact_draw_ir_geometry(
                result, ids[index], "body", tags[index],
                [0, margins[index], WIDTH, font_sizes[index]]
            )
            val node_index = _node_index(
                result.hit_index.nodes, ids[index]
            )
            val style = result.hit_index.styles[node_index]
            expect(style.display).to_equal("block")
            expect(style.bold).to_equal(true)
            expect(style.font_size).to_equal(font_sizes[index])
            expect(style.margin_l).to_equal(0)
            expect(style.margin_t).to_equal(margins[index])
            expect(style.margin_r).to_equal(0)
            expect(style.margin_b).to_equal(margins[index])
            expect(_style(
                _command(result.composition, ids[index]), "font-size"
            )).to_equal(font_sizes[index].to_string())
            val pixels = _render_pixels(result.composition)
            expect(_count_color(
                pixels, colors[index]
            )).to_be_greater_than(0)
            index = index + 1

    # @manual: show
    # @capture(html)
    # @capture(protocol)
    # @capture(gui)
    # @req REQ-WEB-BROWSER-002 REQ-WEB-BROWSER-004
    # @req REQ-WEB-BROWSER-019 REQ-WEB-BROWSER-021
    it "should keep sub and sup in inline flow with distinct baselines":
        step("Trace HTML elements through Web semantics and Draw IR")
        _expect_pinned_html_corpus()
        val html = (
            "<style>html,body{margin:0;font-size:16px}" +
            "body{padding-top:8px}</style><body id='body'>" +
            "<span id='lead'>A</span>" +
            "<sub id='sub' style='background:#dc2626'>B</sub>" +
            "<sup id='sup' style='background:#2563eb'>C</sup></body>"
        )
        val result = simple_web_layout_render_html_draw_ir_result(
            html, WIDTH, HEIGHT
        )
        _expect_semantic_identity(html, "sub", "sub", "body")
        _expect_semantic_identity(html, "sup", "sup", "body")
        _expect_exact_draw_ir_geometry(
            result, "sub", "body", "sub", [8, 12, 7, 13]
        )
        _expect_exact_draw_ir_geometry(
            result, "sup", "body", "sup", [15, 4, 7, 13]
        )
        val lead = _node_index(result.hit_index.nodes, "lead")
        val sub = _node_index(result.hit_index.nodes, "sub")
        val sup = _node_index(result.hit_index.nodes, "sup")
        expect([
            result.hit_index.boxes.bx[lead],
            result.hit_index.boxes.by[lead],
            result.hit_index.boxes.bw[lead],
            result.hit_index.boxes.bh[lead]
        ]).to_equal([0, 8, 8, 16])
        expect(result.hit_index.styles[sub].display).to_equal("inline")
        expect(result.hit_index.styles[sup].display).to_equal("inline")
        expect(result.hit_index.styles[sub].font_size).to_equal(13)
        expect(result.hit_index.styles[sup].font_size).to_equal(13)
        expect(result.hit_index.styles[sub].line_height_px).to_equal(0)
        expect(result.hit_index.styles[sup].line_height_px).to_equal(0)
        expect(result.hit_index.styles[sub].vertical_align).to_equal("sub")
        expect(result.hit_index.styles[sup].vertical_align).to_equal("super")
        expect(result.hit_index.boxes.by[sub]).to_be_greater_than(
            result.hit_index.boxes.by[lead]
        )
        expect(result.hit_index.boxes.by[sup]).to_be_less_than(
            result.hit_index.boxes.by[lead]
        )
        val lead_text = _text_command(result.composition, "A")
        val sub_text = _text_command(result.composition, "B")
        val sup_text = _text_command(result.composition, "C")
        expect([
            lead_text.y, sub_text.y, sup_text.y
        ]).to_equal([8, 12, 4])
        expect(sub_text.y).to_be_greater_than(lead_text.y)
        expect(sup_text.y).to_be_less_than(lead_text.y)
        expect(_style(sub_text, "font-size")).to_equal("13")
        expect(_style(sup_text, "font-size")).to_equal("13")
        expect(_style(
            _command(result.composition, "sub"), "display"
        )).to_equal("inline")
        expect(_style(
            _command(result.composition, "sup"), "vertical-align"
        )).to_equal("super")
        val pixels = _render_pixels(result.composition)
        expect(_count_color(pixels, 0xFFDC2626u32)).to_be_greater_than(0)
        expect(_count_color(pixels, 0xFF2563EBu32)).to_be_greater_than(0)
        val inherited_line_height_html = (
            "<style>html,body{margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:24px}" +
            "</style><body id='line-height-parent'>" +
            "<sub id='normal-line-height-sub'>B</sub></body>"
        )
        val inherited_line_height = simple_web_layout_render_html_draw_ir_result(
            inherited_line_height_html, WIDTH, HEIGHT
        )
        val line_height_parent = _node_index(
            inherited_line_height.hit_index.nodes, "line-height-parent"
        )
        val normal_line_height_sub = _node_index(
            inherited_line_height.hit_index.nodes, "normal-line-height-sub"
        )
        expect(inherited_line_height.hit_index.styles[
            line_height_parent
        ].line_height_px).to_equal(24)
        expect(inherited_line_height.hit_index.styles[
            normal_line_height_sub
        ].line_height_px).to_equal(0)

    # @manual: show
    # @capture(html)
    # @capture(protocol)
    # @capture(gui)
    # @req REQ-WEB-BROWSER-002 REQ-WEB-BROWSER-004
    # @req REQ-WEB-BROWSER-019 REQ-WEB-BROWSER-021
    it "should fail closed for unsupported selectedcontent and render slot fallback inline":
        step("Trace HTML elements through Web semantics and Draw IR")
        _expect_pinned_html_corpus()
        val html = (
            "<style>html,body{margin:0;font-size:16px;" +
            "line-height:16px;color:#111827}" +
            "#slot{{color:#7c3aed}}</style><body id='body'>" +
            "<select id='select'><button id='select-button'>" +
            "<selectedcontent id='selected' style='display:block;width:8px;" +
            "height:8px;background:#dc2626'></selectedcontent></button>" +
            "<option selected>Selected option</option></select>" +
            "<select id='invalid-select'><option>Before</option>" +
            "<button id='late-button'><selectedcontent id='invalid-selected' " +
            "style='background:#16a34a'>" +
            "</selectedcontent></button></select>" +
            "<select id='multiple-select' multiple>" +
            "<button id='multiple-button'>" +
            "<selectedcontent id='multiple-selected' style='background:#0891b2'>" +
            "</selectedcontent></button></select>" +
            "<select id='late-selected-select'><button id='content-button'>" +
            "<span id='button-prefix'></span>" +
            "<selectedcontent id='late-selected' style='background:#ca8a04'>" +
            "</selectedcontent></button></select>" +
            "<div id='slot-control' style='position:absolute;left:0;" +
            "top:32px;width:96px;height:16px'>" +
            "<slot id='slot'>slot-fallback</slot></div></body>"
        )
        val result = simple_web_layout_render_html_draw_ir_result(
            html, WIDTH, HEIGHT
        )
        _expect_semantic_identity(
            html, "selected", "selectedcontent", "select-button"
        )
        _expect_semantic_identity(
            html, "slot", "slot", "slot-control"
        )
        _expect_semantic_identity(
            html, "invalid-selected", "selectedcontent", "late-button"
        )
        _expect_semantic_identity(
            html, "multiple-selected", "selectedcontent", "multiple-button"
        )
        _expect_semantic_identity(
            html, "late-selected", "selectedcontent", "content-button"
        )
        val selected = _node_index(result.hit_index.nodes, "selected")
        val invalid_selected = _node_index(
            result.hit_index.nodes, "invalid-selected"
        )
        val multiple_selected = _node_index(
            result.hit_index.nodes, "multiple-selected"
        )
        val late_selected = _node_index(
            result.hit_index.nodes, "late-selected"
        )
        val slot = _node_index(result.hit_index.nodes, "slot")
        expect(result.hit_index.styles[selected].display).to_equal("none")
        expect(_command_index(result.composition, "selected")).to_equal(-1)
        expect(result.hit_index.styles[invalid_selected].display).to_equal("inline")
        expect(result.hit_index.styles[multiple_selected].display).to_equal("inline")
        expect(result.hit_index.styles[late_selected].display).to_equal("inline")
        expect(_command_index(
            result.composition, "invalid-selected"
        )).to_be_greater_than(-1)
        expect(_command_index(
            result.composition, "multiple-selected"
        )).to_be_greater_than(-1)
        expect(_command_index(
            result.composition, "late-selected"
        )).to_be_greater_than(-1)
        expect(result.hit_index.styles[slot].display).to_equal("inline")
        _expect_exact_draw_ir_geometry(
            result, "slot", "slot-control", "slot", [0, 32, 104, 16]
        )
        expect(_style(
            _command(result.composition, "slot"), "color"
        )).to_equal("4286331629")
        expect(_has_text(
            result.composition, "slot-fallback"
        )).to_equal(true)
        val pixels = _render_pixels(result.composition)
        expect(_count_color(pixels, 0xFFDC2626u32)).to_equal(0)
        expect(_count_color(pixels, 0xFF16A34Au32)).to_be_greater_than(0)
        expect(_count_color(pixels, 0xFF7C3AEDu32)).to_be_greater_than(0)
